      "question": "What is the main connectivity idea introduced by DenseNet?",
      "with_context": "The main connectivity idea introduced by DenseNet is dense connectivity, where any layer receives the feature-maps of all preceding layers as input (file, page 2).",
      "without_context": "The main connectivity idea introduced by DenseNet is the use of dense connections, which are connections between any two layers in the network, not just the next layer in the sequence. This allows the network to capture long-range dependencies and relationships between different parts of the input data, which can lead to improved performance and robustness."
