      "without_context": "Grad-CAM (Gradient-weighted Class Activation Mapping) is a technique used in computer vision to visualize the importance of different regions in an image for a specific class or object. It is designed to produce a heatmap or a visual representation of the regions in an image that are most relevant to the class or object of interest.\n\nIn other words, Grad-CAM is used to identify the parts of an image that are most likely to be associated with a particular class or object, such as a person, car, or building. The heatmap produced by Grad-CAM can be used to highlight the most important regions in an image, which can be useful for tasks such as object detection, image classification, and image segmentation."
